# ratstack.sh: the agent-first front door for rat-stack

Chartered 2026-09-21 from Joel's grilling in the rat-stack session. The template's demo app stops being a hello world and becomes the stack's own front door: `apps/mischief` serves `https://ratstack.sh`, the page and MCP you point an agent at to learn and use rat-stack. The site is built from the repo's own files, so it cannot drift from the template it ships in, and a child project clears it by deleting one directory and a few Stack lines.

## Finish line

- `https://ratstack.sh/` returns plain text written for an agent: what rat-stack is, where the law lives, how to add a capability, how to connect the MCP. A client that asks for `text/html` (a browser, a link unfurler) gets a minimal page carrying the same text in a `<pre>` plus Open Graph tags, so a pasted link shows the Rat Stack mark. That page is the only HTML on the site.
- `https://ratstack.sh/mcp` is an Effect `McpServer` over streamable HTTP with tools, resources, and prompts. Every resource body is a file in this repo (`AGENTS.md`, `VISION.md`, `README.md`, the pins, chosen `.brain/resources`). Every prompt is a skill file in this repo, also served as plain text at `/skills/<name>`.
- `isitagentready.com` scans `ratstack.sh` at Level 5 with every applicable check passing; checks that do not apply (commerce, auth) are listed with the reason in the site's own `llms.txt`.
- The Worker is `apps/mischief`, declared in the single Stack in `apps/infra`, runs locally with `alchemy dev` in workerd, and ships with `pnpm infra:deploy` from a machine with the Alchemy profile. CI proves the fetch handler with tests; a smoke script proves the deploy and prints the scan level.
- Maintained: the README's keep-or-cut table has a row for clearing it; `AGENTS.md` Project law says product capabilities live in `core` and the demo owns its own; the template acceptance receipt in the Brain includes the deploy and scan.

## Vocabulary

- **mischief** — the app at `apps/mischief` (a group of rats); also the Cloudflare Worker name `Mischief`.
- **agent-first page** — a plain-text body served with `text/markdown` or `text/plain`, written for an agent to read first and a human second.
- **resource** — an MCP resource whose body is one file from this repo, never authored separately.
- **skill** — a `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` file in this repo, served as an MCP prompt and at `/skills/<name>`, installable by any harness that reads a skills directory.
- **projection** — as in `packages/capability`: the same capability appearing as an MCP tool, an HTTP route with OpenAPI, or a CLI command.
- **The human face** (added 2026-09-22, Joel): a request with `Accept: text/html` gets the same content rendered as a page, not a `<pre>` shell: SvelteKit on the same Worker at the newest published kit and Svelte 5 (Joel: "latest with all the new shit": runes, async Svelte, remote functions where stable), light mode, Dank Mono, markdown rendered with real markup. Agents keep the Markdown, MCP, and code-mode surfaces untouched; the page is a projection of the same generated content.
- **Level 5** — isitagentready.com's top level, "agent-native": Level 4 (robots, sitemap, Link headers, AI rules, Content Signals, markdown negotiation, one integration) plus two of three groups: Web Bot Auth; all four integrations (MCP server card, A2A agent card, agent skills index, API catalog); auth metadata (OAuth discovery or `auth.md`). The 22 checks are the checklist; `llms.txt` is required by this brief, not by the scanner.
- **Stack** — the one `Alchemy.Stack` in `apps/infra/alchemy.run.ts`; every cloud resource is declared there.

## Notes

- Skills every session consults: `effect` and `pi-effect` (source first, `.agent_sources/github.com/Effect-TS/effect` at rc.116); the Alchemy mirror at `.agent_sources/github.com/alchemy-run/alchemy` (`website/src/content/docs/cloudflare/` for Workers, custom domains, local development); `grill-master` conventions for this brief.
- Facts settled at charter: `ratstack.sh` was registered 2026-09-21 17:05 UTC through Cloudflare Registrar, nameservers on Cloudflare, no records yet. Alchemy's Worker takes a `domain` prop that provisions DNS and certificate on an existing zone. `alchemy dev` runs Workers in workerd. Effect `McpServer` ships `layerHttp`, `resource`, and `prompt`. `packages/core` and `packages/capability` import nothing from Node at module level except `sandbox.ts` (`effect/unstable/process`); whether that bundles on workerd is a research question.
- Standing calls (Joel, 2026-09-21): EXTREME plain text for the root page and every resource body. Skills are authored as files and served two ways. One Stack, no second `alchemy.run.ts`. App name `mischief`. The site is what the template serves; the earlier `greet` hello-world capability is dropped in favor of the site's own capabilities (pending the capabilities step).
- Execution authorization (Joel, 2026-09-21): research steps run AFK. The `alchemy dev` prototype and the fetch-handler tests may be built without further approval. The first deploy to `ratstack.sh` and any change under `apps/infra` are confirmed with Joel before running, per `AGENTS.md` Boundaries; after that first confirmation, redeploys inside this effort are authorized.
- Workers do not commit and do not edit this brief; the steering session writes ledger lines at harvest.
- Logo (Joel, 2026-09-21): `assets/ratstack-logo.svg`, a rat on a three-layer stack, cream `#FAF5E9` on charcoal `#262829` with one lime layer. The root page stays plain text for agents; browsers and unfurlers get the HTML shell with `og:image` (Joel, 2026-09-21: "be sure site has a nice og image"). The mark is also the README header and the favicon.

- Font: Dank Mono woff2 (Regular, Bold, Italic) already lives in Joel's joelclaw web apps (`apps/web/app/fonts/`); the SvelteKit shell self-hosts the same files. Check the Dank Mono license text for web embedding on owned sites before the first deploy that ships them (2026-09-22).

## Decision ledger

- [Research the 22 isitagentready checks and their exact fix recipes](./research-agent-ready-checks.svx) — all 22 keys with probes, minimal fixtures, level gates, applicability, and sources in the [asset](./research-agent-ready-checks-asset.svx). Applicable and Worker-served: robots with AI rules and Content Signals, sitemap, Link headers, markdown negotiation at `/`, API catalog, MCP server card, agent-skills index (v0.2.0 with sha256 digests), ARD `ai-catalog.json`. DNS-AID is the one check the Stack owns (SVCB records, DNSSEC). Not honest for this site: OAuth, protected resource, `auth.md` with invented endpoints, an A2A card without an `/a2a` service, WebMCP without an HTML page, Web Bot Auth without outbound signing, every commerce check. Consequence: honest Level 5 needs a decision (see the not-applicable step). Scanner drift noted: `llms.txt` is not among the 22 keys.
- [Research Effect McpServer over streamable HTTP with resources and prompts](./research-effect-mcp-over-http.svx) — `layerHttp` options, static and templated `resource`, `prompt`, `instructions` and `websiteUrl`, the SKILL.md-to-prompt mapping, a scanner-compatible server card, and a passing in-memory example over `HttpRouter.toWebHandler`, all in the [asset](./research-effect-mcp-over-http-asset.svx). The finding that matters: of the five protocol adapters at rc.116 only `McpProtocol.v2026_07_28` is request-stateless; `2024-11-05` through `2025-11-25` keep sessions in process memory, which is not safe across Worker isolates. So the Worker serves `2026_07_28` alone, or owns session state in a Durable Object. Which clients speak `2026-07-28` is now its own step.
- [Research the Alchemy Effect Worker shape, custom domain, and local dev at beta.79](./research-alchemy-effect-worker.svx) — the [asset](./research-alchemy-effect-worker-asset.svx) has a copy-ready Effect Worker with `HttpRouter` and `McpServer.layerHttp` inside `fetch`, the single-Stack declaration with `domain: "ratstack.sh"` and explicit adoption of the existing zone, the Alchemy DNS record shape (for DNS-AID), `alchemy dev` behavior in workerd, and the smallest `@effect/vitest` fetch test. Bundling verdict with scratch receipts: importing the `@rat-stack/capability` barrel keeps sandbox residue and roughly doubles the bundle even when only `toToolkit` is used; `mischief` imports worker-safe subpaths `@rat-stack/capability/define` and `/toolkit` instead, so Worker resolution never reaches `sandbox.ts`. A live workerd boot of the barrel was not run; the subpaths make the question moot.
- [Make the Open Graph image and the HTML shell that carries it](./make-og-image.svx) — `apps/mischief/public/og.png` (1200 by 630), `icon-512.png`, `favicon-32.png` rendered from the mark with re-runnable ImageMagick commands in the [asset](./make-og-image-asset.svx), plus the one HTML shell template (`<title>`, `og:title`, `og:description`, absolute `og:image`, `og:url`, `twitter:card` `summary_large_image`, body in `<pre>`), exercised once through a local server.
- [Research which MCP clients speak protocol 2026-07-28, and the Durable Object fallback](./research-mcp-client-protocol-support.svx) — wire-probed on this machine: Claude Code 2.1.278 negotiates `2026-07-28` over HTTP; Cursor 2026.09.18 and the `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` 1.30.0 client stop at `2025-11-25`; Codex CLI 0.155.0 sends `2025-06-18`; Pi's adapter 2.34.0 and MCP Inspector 2.7.0 default to `2025-11-25` but can opt into `2026-07-28` by config. The [asset](./research-mcp-client-protocol-support-asset.svx) sketches a hybrid: stateless Worker for modern clients, one named Durable Object owning Effect's stateful runtime for legacy sessions, with the durability limit (an activation restart drops sessions) and a sunset. Whether to build that is now a grilling step.
- [Decide the site's capabilities](./decide-site-capabilities.svx) — Joel: `search`, `read`, and `execute`, all three, day one. `greet` stays dead. `execute` forces a Worker-side `Sandbox` layer (the subprocess one cannot run in workerd), researched in [research-worker-sandbox](./research-worker-sandbox.svx) before the prototype grows the tools.
- [Research how ratstack.sh runs code-mode programs inside Cloudflare](./research-worker-sandbox.svx) — verdict in the [asset](./research-worker-sandbox-asset.svx): Cloudflare Dynamic Workers through Alchemy's first-class `Cloudflare.WorkerLoader` binding, one fresh isolate per `execute`, `globalOutbound: null`, the program's `tools.<name>()` calls reaching the host over Workers RPC through an `RpcTarget` dispatcher, explicit `cpuMs` and wall timeouts. Proven locally with `wrangler dev --local` and no Cloudflare login: success, guest throw, timeout, and blocked `fetch` all behaved (compatibility date had to be pinned to 2026-05-28 for the bundled workerd). Containers and Workers for Platforms rejected; QuickJS in Wasm is the fallback. Prerequisite seam: split `sandbox.ts` into the Worker-safe service contract and the Node subprocess runner, with a `@rat-stack/capability/sandbox` subpath. Cost note for the deploy step: Dynamic Workers are open beta on Workers Paid (USD 5 monthly minimum).
- [Decide the public content set](./decide-public-content-set.svx) — Joel: skills are site content, catalogue first (the shape of `aihero.dev/skills`). Root leads with `npx skills add joelhooks/rat-stack` and the grouped skills, then Law (the seven repo files, pins generated), then MCP. Skills at `/skills/<name>` and as MCP prompts; law files as MCP resources; `llms-full.txt` concatenates everything. Four skills day one: `learn-rat-stack`, `add-a-capability`, `add-a-lifecycle-machine`, `keep-or-cut`.

- [Write the four skills ratstack.sh ships](./write-skills.svx) — `skills/{learn-rat-stack,add-a-capability,add-a-lifecycle-machine,keep-or-cut}/SKILL.md` (55, 85, 118, 98 lines), every claim from `AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, `VISION.md`, or `packages/*/src`; `add-a-capability` names the current registry honestly (the `capabilities` tuple in `packages/core/src/inspect-file.ts`) rather than inventing a registry module. Oxfmt and the full gate pass on the skills.
- [Build the tools, catalogue, and well-known documents into the Mischief Worker](./build-mischief-tools.svx) — `search`, `read`, `execute` on `/mcp` and `/api` with `/openapi.json`; `execute` runs in a fresh Dynamic Worker through the `CODE_SANDBOX` WorkerLoader binding and a real local run returned a `read` result from a `search`; catalogue root with install line and Link headers, `/skills/<name>`, `llms.txt` and `llms-full.txt`, agent-skills index with digests, api-catalog, `mcp.json`, sitemap; compatibility date pinned to 2026-05-28 for Alchemy's bundled workerd. Capability seam: `./sandbox`, `./code-mode`, `./http-api` subpaths. Gate 19 tasks, six Mischief tests. Not deployed: the WorkerLoader binding needs Workers Paid (open question).
- [Deploy the mischief Worker to ratstack.sh](./deploy-ratstack-sh.svx) — v0 live 2026-09-21: the prototype at `https://ratstack.sh` (root, HTML shell with OG image, `llms.txt`, `robots.txt`, `www` redirect, MCP on `2026-07-28` with the law resource and one prompt). Zone adopted, R2 placeholder removed, stage `prod`, deployed from a clean rift of `main`. Step stays open for the smoke script; tools and catalogue ship as v0.1.
- v0.1 live 2026-09-22: `search`, `read`, `execute` (Dynamic Worker, network blocked, verified in production), catalogue root, skills, every well-known document. Live scan 4/5 Agent-Integrated. Workers Paid confirmed by Joel. Level 5 waits on the two open decisions.

- [Decide how ratstack.sh serves MCP clients that do not speak 2026-07-28](./decide-legacy-mcp-sessions.svx) — `2026-07-28` only; a plain version note at `/mcp` and in `llms.txt`; the Durable Object hybrid stays on the shelf until a scan or a user shows an agent failing.
- [Decide the not-applicable checks](./decide-not-applicable-checks.svx) — Level 5 through a real minimal A2A endpoint (group b) plus an honest anonymous `auth.md` if the scanner counts it (group c), else a Web Bot Auth key directory with a real key (group a); never fake OAuth. DNS-AID and ARD are applicable and still owed. WebMCP and commerce stay out.
- Rate limiting (2026-09-22, Joel: "we likely want rate limiting protection"): each `execute` is one billable Dynamic Worker (`load()` counts per invocation; 1,000 free per month, then USD 0.002 per worker per day) with a 100 ms CPU cap, so the exposure is call volume, not per-call cost. Protection in [protect-and-polish](./protect-and-polish.svx) via Alchemy's `RateLimit` Worker binding.

- The human face (2026-09-22, Joel: "dank mono, light mode, more rendered markdown markup style, sveltekit if possible"): feasible. Alchemy beta.79 ships `Cloudflare.Website.SvelteKit` (wrangler-free adapter, bindings on `platform.env`, HMR dev) with a runnable example; Dank Mono woff2 is on disk. Shape decided in [research-sveltekit-shell](./research-sveltekit-shell.svx), built in [build-sveltekit-shell](./build-sveltekit-shell.svx) after the rate-limit and Level 5 harvests land, since all three touch `apps/mischief`.

- [Rate-limit execute and the MCP surface; polish](./protect-and-polish.svx) — three `RateLimit` bindings live (numeric namespace ids; Cloudflare rejects strings even though Alchemy's type allows them). Measured in production: permissive across connections, strict on one connection, as Cloudflare documents. Not a hard cap; the billing alarm is. `pnpm mischief:smoke` prints the scan level.
- [Reach Level 5](./reach-level-five.svx) — **5/5 Agent-Native on 2026-09-22** via the real `/a2a` endpoint plus the honest anonymous `auth.md`; the scanner counted it, so the Web Bot Auth directory stayed off. DNS-AID records live; DS at the `.sh` parent pending, watched. [Scan asset](./reach-level-five-asset.svx).
- [Deploy](./deploy-ratstack-sh.svx) closed at v0.2.

- [Research the SvelteKit shell on the same Worker](./research-sveltekit-shell.svx) — one `Cloudflare.Website.SvelteKit` Worker; `hooks.server.ts` hands every non-HTML request and every agent path to the existing Effect web handler unchanged, HTML on `/`, `/skills`, `/skills/<name>` goes to SvelteKit; bindings move to the Website's `env` and `platform.env` is typed by `InferEnv`; markdown rendered at generate time with `marked`; pages stay dynamic. Pins: Kit `3.0.0-next.27` (prerelease; npm latest is still Kit 2), Svelte `5.57.1`, Vite `8.3.0`, `svelte-check` `4.7.6`, `@alchemy.run/frontend-frameworks` `2.0.0-beta.79`. Wrinkle: Kit v3 cannot run `svelte-kit sync` on TypeScript 7 (calls the removed `ts.sys`), so `apps/mischief` carries a TypeScript `6.0.3` island for Kit and `svelte-check`, while the root TS7 plus Effect diagnostics keep checking every `.ts` seam through a second tsconfig. Runes yes; async Svelte and remote functions are experimental at these pins and stay off. Spike passed under `alchemy dev` without login (fake local-only credentials were needed; beta.79 ergonomics bug). Dank Mono: the woff2 files are genuine, embedded license says all rights reserved, EULA URL was down; Joel already self-hosts the same files on joelclaw.com, so they ship here on that precedent unless he says otherwise. [Asset](./research-sveltekit-shell-asset.svx).

- Superseded SvelteKit experiment (2026-09-22): Joel required TypeScript 7 only, so Kit next.27 needed a small config-API compatibility patch and `@rsvelte/svelte-check --no-type-check`. Production exposed a second incompatibility: Alchemy beta.79 still called Kit 3's removed `generateManifest` adapter API. A compatibility patch made the HTML deploy, but MCP then threw Cloudflare 1101 while static and HTML routes worked. The launch smoke caught it.
- Plain HTML decision (2026-09-22, Joel: "plain html 86 sveltkit wanking"): SvelteKit, its adapter, its checker, Vite app config, components, routes, generated state, and both patches are gone. The single Effect Worker now negotiates static build-generated HTML for `/`, `/skills`, and known skill pages while preserving exact Markdown for agent requests. `src/html.ts` owns the document shell. A final taste pass removed all CSS, fonts, logos, favicons, OG images, image metadata, and the Worker asset binding. The human pages use browser-default semantic HTML and ship no application JavaScript.

## Latent

- Deploy from CI with a scoped Cloudflare token, so a merge to `main` redeploys the site; today deploy is manual from a machine with the profile.
- Content freshness: the site reads repo files at bundle time, so every doc change needs a redeploy until CI deploys.
- A human-facing website (`Cloudflare.Website.*`) beside the Worker, later.
- `capnp-es` under alchemy wants TypeScript 5 or 6; harmless so far.
- Spend alarm (2026-09-22, Joel: "don't need a spend limit but if you can set"): Cloudflare `billing_budget_alert` policy `f7f7ce9fd31f4e6e9dd4bb3b8f087ea2`, "ratstack.sh spend alarm (25 USD)", emailing the same address as the account's auto-created 10 USD alert, created through Executor's saved Cloudflare connection and read back. The 10 USD default policy stays and will fire on Workers Paid alone.
- Strict execute cap: if the billing alarm ever fires or abuse shows, replace the per-isolate `RateLimit` counters with a Durable Object counter (per IP and global) in front of `execute`; the bindings stay as the cheap first line.
- DNSSEC: DS at the `.sh` parent should appear on its own (Cloudflare Registrar); if the watch expires without it, enable the DS from the registrar panel by hand.
- Legacy-protocol sunset: when the hybrid exists, the evidence to drop the Durable Object is a client matrix where every likely client defaults to `2026-07-28`.
- Whether `apps/mischief` also gets a CLI projection (`pnpm mischief search ...`) for local use of the same capabilities.

- Cloudflare CI (checked 2026-09-22, Joel asked): `github.com/cloudflare/ci` is the `@cloudflare/ci` library (0.2.0, 2026-09-14), a CI engine you deploy as your own Worker on Workflows plus a Sandbox container; not a hosted product with an API to adopt. Alchemy beta.79 has no mention of it (zero code or issue hits upstream), but it can declare almost every piece the example Worker needs: Worker with `nodejs_compat`, Containers, sqlite Durable Objects, Workflows, Queues, R2, and Artifacts namespaces and bindings. The one gap found: the example's `triggers.events` (`cf.artifacts.repo.pushed` targeting a workflow); nothing in `Workflows/Workflow.ts` declares event triggers. Workaround if ever wanted: a push webhook route that calls `CI_WORKFLOW.create()`. Not part of this effort; GitHub Actions stays the gate.

## Out of scope

- Auth, analytics, and every commerce protocol on day one (Joel, 2026-09-21). They return only as a fresh effort if the finish line is redrawn. The human-facing page left this list on 2026-09-22 when Joel redrew the finish line (see The human face); it is a projection of the same generated content, not a separate site.
